This is a Svelte 5 project, so use the guidance in cursor/svelte-llms.md when needed to guide changes

## Svelte 5 rules
For the new app, always use Svelte 5 syntax.
Svelte 5 gotchas:
- on:click is now onclick, on:mouseover is now onmouseover, etc.
- the `$state` rune is only available inside `.svelte` and `.svelte.js/ts` files.
- onclick|stopPropagation does not work (using vertical bar is not allowed in this context)
- use `let { post } = $props();` instead of `export let post;`

### Typescript
Use TypeScript only sparingly e.g. for complex bespoke objects but avoid being overly verbose e.g. we don't need to mark-up type for HTML events etc.
Data structures are defined using TypeScript in /src/lib/types/game.d.ts - make sure you use these as reference and keep these up-to-date.

### Styling
Always use TailwindCSS unless something very specific is required that Tailwind cannot handle.

### Utilities
Utilities and pure functions live under /src/libs
Import with e.g.:
import { chapters } from '$lib/chapters';

### State management
Use Svelte stores for managing state, and store these under /src/stores e.g.

```js
// $stores/user.svelte.js
class UserStore {
  var user = $state();
}
export const userStore = new UserStore();
```

## Use of forms
In general, avoid using <form> tags instead use inputs / selects etc that are bound to variables or parts of an object.
If forms must be used, note that Svelte does not like vertical bars e.g. 'onsubmit|preventDefault' is not a valid attribute name.

### ENV vars
Environment variables should be imported individually, e.g.:
```js
  import { PUBLIC_WS_ENDPOINT, ANOTHER_VAR } from '$env/static/public';
  import { A_PRIVATE_VAR } from '$env/static/private';
  console.log(PUBLIC_WS_ENDPOINT);
```

## TROUBLESHOOTING
When passing Svelte 5 $state variables to native bridged code you can get a "DataCloneError: The object can not be cloned." error so you need to use the ... spread operator to copy the object (see: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79317063/state-object-could-not-be-cloned )
